From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:49:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] android: honor explicit camera orientation configuration

The sensor's libcamera rotation property is also used to request native
capture buffers from the simple pipeline. Keep that pipeline orientation
unchanged, but allow an explicit per-device HAL configuration to override
the Android-facing mounting metadata.

Otherwise the HAL only warns about a conflicting configured rotation and
ignores it. ThinkSmart needs Android orientation 270 rather than the
sensor-derived 90 to avoid inverted front-camera preview and photographs.
---
Base-commit: 3becb16c1fa22d79a4d7eeb75a36fc895b4b7abf

 src/android/camera_device.cpp |    9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/android/camera_device.cpp b/src/android/camera_device.cpp
--- a/src/android/camera_device.cpp
+++ b/src/android/camera_device.cpp
@@ -360,6 +360,9 @@
 	 * rotation property in anticlockwise direction. Read the libcamera's
 	 * rotation property (anticlockwise) and compute the corresponding
 	 * value for clockwise direction as required by the Android orientation
 	 * metadata.
+	 *
+	 * A per-device HAL configuration may override the Android metadata
+	 * without changing the sensor's native buffer orientation.
 	 */
 	const auto &rotation = properties.get(properties::Rotation);
@@ -367,9 +370,11 @@
 		orientation_ = (360 - *rotation) % 360;
 		if (cameraConfigData && cameraConfigData->rotation != -1 &&
 		    orientation_ != cameraConfigData->rotation) {
 			LOG(HAL, Warning)
-				<< "Camera orientation does not match"
-				<< " configuration file. Using " << orientation_;
+				<< "Using configured camera orientation "
+				<< cameraConfigData->rotation
+				<< " instead of sensor-derived " << orientation_;
+			orientation_ = cameraConfigData->rotation;
 		}
 	} else if (cameraConfigData) {
 		if (cameraConfigData->rotation == -1) {
